      "message": "You should not need this cast. Refer to the definition of eventuallyExpect :\n\n    fun \u003cT : CallbackEntry\u003e eventuallyExpect(\n        type: KClass\u003cT\u003e,\n        timeoutMs: Long \u003d defaultTimeoutMs,\n        predicate: (cb: T) -\u003e Boolean \u003d { true }\n    )\n\n`type` is a `KClass\u003cT\u003e`, and you\u0027re passing `NETWORK_CAPS_UPDATED` which is a `KClass\u003cCapabilitiesChanged\u003e`. The compiler should therefore infer that `T` is a `CapabilitiesChanged`. Now, in the predicate, the argument is a `T` which means `entry` is already a `CapabilitiesChanged`. You should therefore not need the cast : the compiler should let you call `entry.getCaps()` without it.\n\n\n(the same applies to l.845, if you feel like fixing it at the same time)",
